    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 22nd with a high-floor lineup, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who earns today\u2019s top efficiency rating of 82.13. His matchup against Senga is the highlight of the day; the combination of a favorable SP_xERA of 4.75 and a substantial +14% dynamic platoon advantage makes him an elite play. **Christian Yelich** also projects exceptionally well at 74.33 against Singer, buoyed by a strong +13% platoon edge and the leadoff spot. Meanwhile, **Caleb Durbin** remains a crucial engine for our stolen base production, seeing his score climb to 72.77 due to a park-factor boost and favorable wind conditions that should aid his offensive profile against Feltner.\n\nOur most difficult decision came at the margins, where **Chase Meidroth** (44.13) fell just short of a starting berth. While his profile was competitive, the optimizer favored the positional versatility and higher scoring ceilings provided by the middle infielders already in play. We continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, **Rece Hinds**, and **Zac Veen**, all of whom remain in the minors and are unavailable for the active rotation today. \n\nStrategic risks remain, particularly regarding **Yordan Alvarez** and **Kazuma Okamoto**. **Yordan Alvarez** faces a stiff test against Cease; while his elite xwOBA of 0.447 provides comfort, his score is tempered by a significant -19% penalty due to the opponent's high skill level. Similarly, **Kazuma Okamoto** is a marginal start today (43.05) as he deals with a tough matchup against Brown. Conversely, **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** are well-positioned against Griffin, but we will watch closely for any late-breaking weather or lineup changes, as their value is heavily tied to the top-of-the-order run-scoring environment.",
